{
  "name": "pre-read-after-an-ended-subagents-stale-arm-read-and-a-peer-commit-is-denied",
  "description": "#514 with #525: a Read admitted on the stale arm uses up the recovery. Subagent a0826622451ec196f of session 44444444 reads v1 and B commits v2, which makes its copy INVALID; its Read of the v2 bytes is denied, which arms its recovery. Its stop then carries \"ended\": true, which forgets its rows but not the recovery. Its next Read of the v2 bytes finds no row and offers the recorded bytes, so it is admitted with the stale-read warning and re-granted SHARED at v2. B commits v3. The subagent's Read of the v3 bytes is denied with the commit text; prior_version_seen_by_session is 2, the version its admitted Read was granted at. Before the fix the Python coordinator kept the recovery through the stale-arm re-grant and admitted this Read with no deny; the Node coordinator already dropped it there. Timestamps vary per run; the reason bytes and the summary are the contract.",
